WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.137
Step three reads what the
code hands to Chapter 6.

2
00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:08.491
The two requests that passed become
two rows of the replatform file:

3
00:00:08.491 --> 00:00:12.601
a D M S A for the billing account
and a G M S A for payroll.

4
00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:16.097
Check that both rows carry a
request I D and a change record:

5
00:00:16.097 --> 00:00:20.250
the SailPoint request and the
ServiceNow change that approved them.

6
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.974
The retrievers file has one entry,

7
00:00:22.974 --> 00:00:26.963
for the payroll G M S A,
naming its one group of hosts.

8
00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:33.675
The D M S A has no entry, because a D M S
A learns its hosts during its migration.

9
00:00:33.675 --> 00:00:38.980
These files go into Chapter 6's reviewed
inputs in a reviewed pull request,

10
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.850
and Chapter 6's plan refuses a write
with no request or change record.

11
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.580
So the plan creates
exactly what was approved.
